# Add patterns of files dvc should ignore, which could improve
# the performance. Learn more at
# https://dvc.org/doc/user-guide/dvcignore

# --- `--tiny` smoke artifacts are not experiment data ---
# The CPU smoke overlay (configs/tiny.yaml, via `--tiny`) suffixes every run
# name with "-tiny", so its checkpoints and metrics are name-identifiable. They
# regenerate in seconds (`just train exp=e3 --tiny`), carry no readout anyone
# would cite, and would otherwise push multi-MB blobs to R2 for nothing.
#
# scripts/run_ladder.sh already skips `dvc add`/`dvc push` on tiny runs; this is
# the other half of that intent, covering the manual path. Listing them here
# makes `dvc add models/e3-tiny-final.pt` FAIL LOUDLY rather than quietly
# tracking a smoke artifact as if it were data.
models/*-tiny-*.pt
results/*-tiny.jsonl
